FOUND: The tour : A guided path for a first visit, one page a stop with Back and Next: the three tools, the grid, research, the price board and the digest, then the whole country: its regions, a storm across it, demand, trade, the resource map, where energy goes, the energy of AI, every state and grid conditions.
FOUND: The tour : A guided path for a first visit, one page a stop with Back and Next: the three tools, the grid, research, the price board and the digest, then the whole country: its regions, a storm across it, demand, trade, the resource map, where energy goes, the energy of AI, every state and grid conditions. What is on a bill : Five real electricity bills built line by line from the tariffs (PG&E, SCE and SDG&E in California; Oncor and CenterPoint in Texas), and how much of each is the wholesale price of energy.
FOUND: Thesis Builder : Type a niche and get a sourced market report of it: scope and definitions, five trends each drawn with a real series, capital, incumbents, risks, policy and timing, every figure with its source; the company landscape, deal funnel and pipeline fill from a data provider's answer you paste from your own account.
FOUND: Thesis Builder : Type a niche and get a sourced market report of it: scope and definitions, five trends each drawn with a real series, capital, incumbents, risks, policy and timing, every figure with its source; the company landscape, deal funnel and pipeline fill from a data provider's answer you paste from your own account. Internal. Games Home battery game : Run a home battery through a real day of ERCOT prices: charge cheap, sell dear, answer the fleet call, and see what perfect foresight would have earned.
FOUND: Every number is checked against the fetched sources its row cites. A short cell whose number is not found there is replaced by "not confirmed".
FOUND: A sentence (40 characters or more) keeps its words and its numbers and is followed by "(not confirmed: ...)", naming each number no cited source holds, so the reader sees both the sentence and which of its numbers no source gives (session 10236's audit counted 80 such numbers in 49 texts of the five runs saved on 6 October 2026).
FOUND: After a sentence, "(not confirmed: ...)" names the numbers in it that no cited source holds not held yet The ERW has no source for this PitchBook pending Asked of PitchBook; shown when the PitchBook answer is submitted Each placeholder says why on hover.
FOUND: Which companies are on the map This section and the next describe a run written before 9 October 2026. A run since then searches for no company: its company tabs hold only what a data provider's pasted answer gives, labeled with the provider's name, with no score of the ERW's.
FOUND: In such a run companies came from three places: the ERW's own companies and deals tables, web search, and PitchBook (below).
FOUND: The confidence score In a run written before 9 October 2026, each company has a score from 0 to 100 that says how well documented it is, with one line beside it saying what it rests on.
